{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "error (ambiguous): \"even\"\nambiguous: set args.assume.question to one of:\n  1) an even function, f(-x) = f(x) (default)\n  2) an even number for every input\nrepeat the request with args.assume.question set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"an odd function\" or \"always odd\""}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": false, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x squared even?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": [], "understood": false}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "", "error": {"code": "ambiguous", "message": "\"even\"", "key": "question", "readings": [{"index": 1, "reading": "an even function, f(-x) = f(x)", "default": true}, {"index": 2, "reading": "an even number for every input", "default": false}], "how": "repeat the request with args.assume.question set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default; or: say \"an odd function\" or \"always odd\""}}, "isError": true}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: parity it\nparity of it:\n  even: f(-x) = f(x)\n  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x squared even?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = x^2", "parity it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "parity", "even": "f(-x) = f(x)", "proved_symbolically_parity_rules": "x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)", "headline": "parity of it:"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "\"even\": an even function, f(-x) = f(x) (args.assume.question)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: parity it\nparity of it:\n  even: f(-x) = f(x)\n  proved symbolically (parity rules: x is odd; sums keep a common parity, products multiply it; sin/tan/atan preserve it, cos/abs make it even)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "error (ambiguous): x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body\nambiguous: set args.assume.untyped to one of:\n  1) inferred (default): assume.untyped = \"inferred\"\n  2) real: give the type (params[].type, or x: real in the text)\nrepeat the request with args.assume.untyped set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default\n\n  note: even for every input when the range is 0..0\n  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: lhs(x) = it(x) % 2\n  ucas: range lhs\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": false, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x squared even?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = x^2", "lhs(x) = it(x) % 2", "range lhs"], "understood": true}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "\"even\": an even number for every input (args.assume.question)"}, {"kind": "info", "text": "even for every input when the range is 0..0"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: even for every input when the range is 0..0\n  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: lhs(x) = it(x) % 2\n  ucas: range lhs\n", "error": {"code": "ambiguous", "message": "x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body", "key": "untyped", "readings": [{"index": 1, "reading": "inferred", "default": true, "how": "assume.untyped = \"inferred\""}, {"index": 2, "reading": "real", "default": false, "how": "give the type (params[].type, or x: real in the text)"}], "how": "repeat the request with args.assume.untyped set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default"}}, "isError": true}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: even for every input when the range is 0..0\n  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: lhs(x) = it(x) % 2\n  ucas: range lhs\n  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body\n  note: argument 1 of it converted from int to real\nrange of lhs -> real:\n  [0, 1]\n  sampled 65536 points (domain has 2^64 or more points); not exhaustive\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "is x squared even?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x) = x^2", "lhs(x) = it(x) % 2", "range lhs"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "range", "type": "real", "empty": false, "exhaustive": false, "points": 65536, "undefined_points": 0, "nan_points": 0, "inf_points": 0, "min": 0, "max": 1}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "\"even\": an even number for every input (args.assume.question)"}, {"kind": "assumed", "text": "x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body"}, {"kind": "info", "text": "even for every input when the range is 0..0"}, {"kind": "info", "text": "argument 1 of it converted from int to real"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "a sample of the domain"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: even for every input when the range is 0..0\n  ucas: it(x) = x^2\n  ucas: lhs(x) = it(x) % 2\n  ucas: range lhs\n  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body\n  note: argument 1 of it converted from int to real\nrange of lhs -> real:\n  [0, 1]\n  sampled 65536 points (domain has 2^64 or more points); not exhaustive\n"}, "isError": false}}
